var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"location":"auth/#auth","page":"Authentication","title":"Authentication","text":"The GoogleAuth package implements Google Cloud authentication:\n\nApplication Default Credentials (ADC) — reads ~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json\nService Account JWT — signs JWTs with an RSA private key from a JSON key file\nCompute Engine metadata — fetches tokens from the GCE metadata server\nBrowser OAuth 2.0 — PKCE installed-app flow for interactive use\nWorkload Identity Federation — exchanges external OIDC tokens (e.g. GitHub Actions) for Google access tokens, keylessly\n\nAll credential types share the Credentials abstract interface and are automatically wrapped in CachedCredentials for token caching.","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#Types","page":"Authentication","title":"Types","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#Functions","page":"Authentication","title":"Functions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#Examples","page":"Authentication","title":"Examples","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#ADC-(most-common)","page":"Authentication","title":"ADC (most common)","text":"import GoogleAuth\n\ncreds = GoogleAuth.get_application_default()\ntoken = GoogleAuth.get_token(creds)\nprintln(token.token_type)   # \"Bearer\"","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#Service-Account","page":"Authentication","title":"Service Account","text":"import JSON, GoogleAuth\n\nsa = GoogleAuth.ServiceAccountCredentials(JSON.parse(read(\"key.json\", String)))\ncreds = GoogleAuth.CachedCredentials(sa)","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#Browser-(interactive-/-installed-app)","page":"Authentication","title":"Browser (interactive / installed-app)","text":"import GoogleAuth\n\n# Opens the browser for the user to log in; credentials are returned in memory.\ncreds = GoogleAuth.authorize_via_browser()","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#Workload-Identity-Federation-(GitHub-Actions,-keyless)","page":"Authentication","title":"Workload Identity Federation (GitHub Actions, keyless)","text":"Workload Identity Federation lets CI systems authenticate to Google Cloud without long-lived service account keys. With GitHub Actions, use the google-github-actions/auth action — it writes an external_account JSON file and sets GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS, so ADC just works:\n\n# .github/workflows/deploy.yml\npermissions:\n  id-token: write   # required for OIDC\n  contents: read\n\nsteps:\n  - uses: google-github-actions/auth@v2\n    with:\n      workload_identity_provider: projects/123/locations/global/workloadIdentityPools/pool/providers/github\n      service_account: deploy@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com\n  - run: julia my_script.jl   # get_application_default() picks up WIF automatically\n\nimport GoogleAuth\n\n# Inside the workflow, no code changes are needed:\ncreds = GoogleAuth.get_application_default()\n# creds isa CachedCredentials{ExternalAccountCredentials}\n\nFile- and url-sourced external credentials are supported (with optional JSON field extraction). AWS and executable credential sources are not implemented.","category":"section"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.Credentials","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.Credentials","text":"Abstract type for Google Cloud credentials.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.Token","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.Token","text":"Represents an OAuth 2.0 access token.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.UserCredentials","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.UserCredentials","text":"User Credentials (loaded from gcloud auth application-default login).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.ServiceAccountCredentials","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.ServiceAccountCredentials","text":"Service Account Credentials (loaded from a JSON key file).\n\nUse with_scopes(creds, scopes) to attach OAuth scopes before wrapping in CachedCredentials; scopes baked into the struct are used by get_token.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.ComputeCredentials","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.ComputeCredentials","text":"Compute Engine Metadata Credentials (used for Workload Identity / GCE).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.CachedCredentials","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.CachedCredentials","text":"CachedCredentials(inner)\n\nWraps any Credentials subtype and caches the access token until it is within 5 minutes of expiry, then fetches a fresh one automatically. Thread-safe: concurrent callers share a single ReentrantLock.\n\nget_application_default() returns a CachedCredentials-wrapped value by default. You can also wrap manually:\n\ncreds = CachedCredentials(with_scopes(sa, [\"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/bigquery\"]))\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.ExternalAccountCredentials","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.ExternalAccountCredentials","text":"ExternalAccountCredentials <: Credentials\n\nWorkload Identity Federation credentials, loaded from an external_account JSON configuration (such as the one written by gcloud iam workload-identity-pools create-cred-config or the google-github-actions/auth action).\n\nget_token performs up to three steps:\n\nFetch the subject token from credential_source — either a local file (\"file\") or an HTTP endpoint (\"url\", with optional headers). When format.type == \"json\", the token is extracted from the field named by format.subject_token_field_name; otherwise the raw content is used.\nExchange it for a Google access token at the STS endpoint (token_url).\nWhen service_account_impersonation_url is present, call generateAccessToken to impersonate the target service account.\n\nOnly file- and url-sourced credentials are supported; AWS (environment_id) and executable sources throw an error at construction.\n\nWrap in CachedCredentials for caching — get_application_default() does this automatically when GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS points at an external_account file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.get_application_default","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.get_application_default","text":"get_application_default() -> CachedCredentials\n\nImplements the Application Default Credentials (ADC) strategy and wraps the result in a CachedCredentials so the token is cached and auto-renewed.\n\nSearch order:\n\nGOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS environment variable.\nWell-known file (~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json).\nCompute Engine / GKE / Cloud Run metadata server.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.get_token","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.get_token","text":"Gets an access token using the given credentials.\n\n\n\n\n\nFetches an access token using UserCredentials (OAuth 2.0 refresh token).\n\n\n\n\n\nFetches an access token using ServiceAccountCredentials via a signed JWT.\n\nScopes are taken from the credentials object (set via with_scopes). If no scopes are set, defaults to https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform.\n\n\n\n\n\nFetches an access token from the Google Cloud metadata server.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.authorization_header","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.authorization_header","text":"Returns an Authorization HTTP header pair (\"Authorization\" => \"Bearer <token>\") for the given credentials. Fetches a fresh access token on every call.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"auth/#GoogleAuth.authorize_via_browser","page":"Authentication","title":"GoogleAuth.authorize_via_browser","text":"authorize_via_browser(; client_id, client_secret, scopes, ...) -> CachedCredentials\n\nRun the Installed-App OAuth 2.0 flow with PKCE:\n\nStart a one-shot HTTP server on bind_host:port (random port by default).\nOpen the user's browser to Google's authorization endpoint (or print the URL when open_browser=false), after the callback listener is already ready.\nWait for Google to redirect back with an authorization code.\nExchange the code for an access + refresh token at the token endpoint.\nWrap the result in CachedCredentials (auto-refreshing).\n\nArguments\n\nclient_id::String         — OAuth client ID (Desktop app type, from GCP Console)\nclient_secret::String     — OAuth client secret\nscopes::Vector{String}    — Requested scopes (defaults to cloud-platform)\nport::Int=0               — Local callback port; 0 requests a free one\nopen_browser::Bool=true   — Open the URL automatically when possible\nbrowser_opener::Function   — Hook for tests/custom launchers (defaults to open_url)\nsave_adc::Bool=false      — Persist the refresh token to the well-known ADC file. Security warning: When true, the refresh token (a long-lived credential that can be used to obtain new access tokens indefinitely) is written in plaintext to ~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json (Linux/macOS) or %APPDATA%\\gcloud\\application_default_credentials.json (Windows). Any process or user that can read that file gains access to your Google Cloud resources. Leave this false (the default) to keep credentials in memory only, valid for the current Julia session.\ntimeout::Real=60          — Seconds to wait for the callback\nbind_host::String=\"127.0.0.1\" — Loopback interface to bind (do NOT use 0.0.0.0)\ntoken_endpoint::String    — Override for testing\nauth_endpoint::String     — Override for testing\n\nReturns\n\nA CachedCredentials{UserCredentials} ready for use with any service client.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"core/#core","page":"Core Library","title":"Core Library","text":"GoogleApiCore provides shared infrastructure used by all service packages: HTTP retry with exponential back-off, AIP-158 pagination, and long-running operation (LRO) support.","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#HTTP-Retry","page":"Core Library","title":"HTTP Retry","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#Example","page":"Core Library","title":"Example","text":"import GoogleApiCore\n\ncfg = GoogleApiCore.RetryConfig(max_attempts=3, initial_delay=0.5)\nresp = GoogleApiCore.do_request_with_retry(\"GET\", \"https://example.com/api\"; config=cfg)","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#Pagination","page":"Core Library","title":"Pagination","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#Example-—-custom-page-type","page":"Core Library","title":"Example — custom page type","text":"import GoogleApiCore\n\nstruct MyPage <: GoogleApiCore.AbstractPage\n    items::Vector{String}\n    next_page_token::Union{String,Nothing}\nend\n\nGoogleApiCore.get_items(p::MyPage)      = p.items\nGoogleApiCore.get_next_token(p::MyPage) = p.next_page_token\n\niter = GoogleApiCore.PagedIterator() do token\n    # call your API here, return a MyPage\nend\n\nfor item in iter\n    println(item)\nend","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#Exceptions","page":"Core Library","title":"Exceptions","text":"Service packages throw these typed exceptions instead of bare error() strings, so callers can catch specific failure categories:","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#Example-2","page":"Core Library","title":"Example","text":"import GoogleApiCore\n\ntry\n    GoogleApiCore.do_request_with_retry(\"GET\", \"https://storage.googleapis.com/...\")\ncatch e\n    if e isa GoogleApiCore.NotFoundError\n        println(\"Object does not exist: \", e.resource)\n    elseif e isa GoogleApiCore.AuthError\n        println(\"Auth failure — check credentials\")\n    elseif e isa GoogleApiCore.GoogleAPIError\n        println(\"API error $(e.status): \", e.message)\n    else\n        rethrow(e)\n    end\nend","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#Long-Running-Operations","page":"Core Library","title":"Long-Running Operations","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.RetryConfig","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.RetryConfig","text":"RetryConfig(; initial_delay=1.0, multiplier=2.0, max_delay=60.0, max_attempts=5)\n\nConfiguration for exponential-backoff retry behaviour.\n\nField Default Meaning\ninitial_delay 1.0 Seconds before the first retry\nmultiplier 2.0 Delay multiplied by this on each subsequent attempt\nmax_delay 60.0 Upper bound on per-attempt sleep time\nmax_attempts 5 Maximum total attempts (including the first)\n\nA 10% random jitter is added to each delay to reduce thundering-herd effects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.do_request_with_retry","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.do_request_with_retry","text":"do_request_with_retry(method, url, headers, body; config, sign!, idempotent, kwargs...)\n\nExecute an HTTP request with exponential backoff and jitter.\n\nThe optional sign! argument is a function (::HTTP.Request) -> Nothing that mutates the request in-place before each attempt — use it to inject auth headers (e.g. req -> CloudBase.GCP.gcpsign!(req; credentials=creds)). The request object is rebuilt from scratch on every retry so that a refreshed token is used automatically.\n\nidempotent=true declares that repeating this request is safe, which enables retry of 429/5xx responses for methods other than GET/PUT (notably POST). A Retry-After header with an integer number of seconds is honoured (capped at config.max_delay).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.AbstractPage","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.AbstractPage","text":"Abstract type for API page responses. A concrete subtype should implement a function to get the next_page_token and the items.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.PagedIterator","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.PagedIterator","text":"A Julia idiomatic iterator over a Google Cloud API that supports AIP-158 Pagination.\n\nExample\n\n# get_items_api should take a page_token and return an AbstractPage\niterator = PagedIterator(page_token -> get_items_api(project, page_token))\nfor item in iterator\n    println(item)\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.get_items","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.get_items","text":"get_items(page::AbstractPage) -> Vector\n\nReturn the list of items contained in the current page. Concrete AbstractPage subtypes must implement this method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.get_next_token","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.get_next_token","text":"get_next_token(page::AbstractPage) -> Union{String, Nothing}\n\nReturn the pagination token for the next page, or nothing if this is the last page. Concrete AbstractPage subtypes must implement this method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.GoogleAPIError","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.GoogleAPIError","text":"GoogleAPIError(status, message)\n\nRaised when a Google Cloud REST API returns an HTTP error status (4xx / 5xx).\n\nFields:\n\nstatus::Int    — HTTP status code\nmessage::String — sanitized error description\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.AuthError","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.AuthError","text":"AuthError(message)\n\nRaised for authentication and authorization failures (e.g. invalid credentials, missing token, or a 401/403 response from the API).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.NotFoundError","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.NotFoundError","text":"NotFoundError(resource)\n\nRaised when the requested resource does not exist (HTTP 404).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.LROperation","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.LROperation","text":"Represents a Google Cloud Long-Running Operation (AIP-151).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.wait_for_operation","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.wait_for_operation","text":"Polls an operation until it completes. This maps the AIP-151 Operation to a Julia Task for asynchronous waiting.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"core/#GoogleApiCore.cancel_operation","page":"Core Library","title":"GoogleApiCore.cancel_operation","text":"Cancels a long running operation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#bigquery","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery API","text":"BigQuery wraps the BigQuery REST API.","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#Client","page":"BigQuery","title":"Client","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#Emulator","page":"BigQuery","title":"Emulator","text":"Set BIGQUERY_EMULATOR_HOST=http://localhost:9050 (or any http:// URL) before constructing a BQClient and it will skip authentication automatically.","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#Query","page":"BigQuery","title":"Query","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#Result-formats","page":"BigQuery","title":"Result formats","text":"query supports two result formats:\n\nformat Return type Notes\n:json (default) Vector{NamedTuple} Compatible with all environments including emulators\n:arrow Arrow.Table Client-side JSON→Arrow conversion; columnar interface\n\n# NamedTuple rows\nrows = BigQuery.query(bq, \"SELECT 1 AS x, 'hi' AS s\")\nrows[1].x   # 1\nrows[1].s   # \"hi\"\n\n# Arrow.Table (columnar)\ntbl = BigQuery.query(bq, \"SELECT 1 AS x UNION ALL SELECT 2\"; format=:arrow)\ncollect(tbl.x)   # [1, 2]","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#Datasets","page":"BigQuery","title":"Datasets","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#Tables","page":"BigQuery","title":"Tables","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#Example","page":"BigQuery","title":"Example","text":"import BigQuery\n\nbq = BigQuery.BQClient(\"my-project\"; location=\"US\")\n\n# Create a dataset and table\nds = BigQuery.create_dataset(bq, \"myds\"; location=\"US\")\n\nschema = [\n    BigQuery.TableFieldSchema(\"id\",   \"INT64\";  mode=\"REQUIRED\"),\n    BigQuery.TableFieldSchema(\"name\", \"STRING\"),\n]\nt = BigQuery.create_table(bq, \"myds\", \"mytable\", schema)\n\n# Query it\nBigQuery.query(bq, \"\"\"\n    INSERT INTO `my-project.myds.mytable` (id, name)\n    VALUES (1, 'Alice'), (2, 'Bob')\n\"\"\")\n\nrows = BigQuery.query(bq, \"SELECT id, name FROM `my-project.myds.mytable` ORDER BY id\")\nfor r in rows\n    println(r.id, \": \", r.name)\nend\n\n# Clean up\nBigQuery.delete_table(bq, \"myds\", \"mytable\")\nBigQuery.delete_dataset(bq, \"myds\"; delete_contents=true)","category":"section"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.BQClient","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.BQClient","text":"BQClient(project_id; creds=nothing, endpoint=nothing)\n\nA BigQuery REST API client.\n\nIf BIGQUERY_EMULATOR_HOST is set in the environment and endpoint is not explicitly provided, the client targets the emulator with no authentication.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.query","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.query","text":"query(client, sql; params=nothing, format=:json, timeout_ms=10_000,\n      max_results=nothing, poll_timeout=600.0) -> Vector{NamedTuple} | Arrow.Table\n\nExecute a SQL query against BigQuery and return the full result set.\n\nparams: query parameters — pass a Dict for named parameters (referenced as @name in SQL) or a Vector for positional ones (referenced as ?). Prefer parameters over string interpolation to avoid SQL injection. DateTime parameters are sent as TIMESTAMP and interpreted as UTC; pass DATETIME values as Strings instead. See the _bq_param_type docstring for the type mapping.\nformat=:json (default): parse rows from the REST API response into Vector{NamedTuple}. Works for all result sizes supported by jobs.query.\nformat=:arrow: same as :json but converts the result to Arrow.Table client-side. Provides a columnar interface without requiring gRPC.\ntimeout_ms: server-side wait passed to jobs.query (timeoutMs).\npoll_timeout: client-side deadline in seconds for the whole job to complete. Throws GoogleApiCore.TimeoutError when exceeded.\n\nquery(bq, \"SELECT name FROM t WHERE age > @min_age AND city = @city\";\n      params=Dict(\"min_age\" => 20, \"city\" => \"Tokyo\"))\nquery(bq, \"SELECT ? + ?\"; params=[1, 2])\n\nColumn values are converted to Julia types — INT64 → Int64, FLOAT64 → Float64, BOOL → Bool, TIMESTAMP/DATETIME → Dates.DateTime (TIMESTAMP is UTC; both truncate to millisecond precision), DATE → Dates.Date, TIME → Dates.Time, BYTES → Vector{UInt8}, RECORD/STRUCT → nested NamedTuple, REPEATED → Vector. NUMERIC and BIGNUMERIC are kept as lossless Strings (parse explicitly if you can tolerate Float64 rounding); SQL NULL becomes missing. See the _coerce_value docstring for the full table.\n\nNote: true zero-copy Arrow streaming requires the BigQuery Storage Read API (gRPC). That is not implemented in v0.1. See the project issue tracker for the GoogleBigQueryStorage.jl roadmap item.\n\nPages are followed automatically via jobs.getQueryResults.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.Dataset","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.Dataset","text":"Dataset\n\nA BigQuery dataset reference and minimal metadata.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.list_datasets","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.list_datasets","text":"list_datasets(client) -> PagedIterator{Dataset}\n\nIterate over all datasets in the client's project.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.get_dataset","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.get_dataset","text":"get_dataset(client, dataset_id) -> Dataset\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.create_dataset","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.create_dataset","text":"create_dataset(client, dataset_id; location=client.location, friendly_name=nothing) -> Dataset\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.delete_dataset","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.delete_dataset","text":"delete_dataset(client, dataset_id; delete_contents=false) -> Nothing\n\nDelete a dataset. If delete_contents=true, also deletes all tables within it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.TableFieldSchema","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.TableFieldSchema","text":"TableFieldSchema\n\nA column in a BigQuery table schema.\n\nFields:\n\nname::String         — column name\ntype::String         — BigQuery type (e.g. \"STRING\", \"INT64\", \"FLOAT64\", \"BOOL\", \"TIMESTAMP\")\nmode::String         — \"NULLABLE\" (default), \"REQUIRED\", or \"REPEATED\"\ndescription::String? — optional description\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.Table","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.Table","text":"Table\n\nA BigQuery table reference and minimal metadata.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.list_tables","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.list_tables","text":"list_tables(client, dataset_id) -> PagedIterator{Table}\n\nIterate over all tables in a dataset.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.get_table","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.get_table","text":"get_table(client, dataset_id, table_id) -> Table\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.create_table","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.create_table","text":"create_table(client, dataset_id, table_id, schema::Vector{TableFieldSchema}) -> Table\n\nCreate a new empty table with the given schema.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"bigquery/#BigQuery.delete_table","page":"BigQuery","title":"BigQuery.delete_table","text":"delete_table(client, dataset_id, table_id) -> Nothing\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#pubsub","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"Cloud Pub/Sub API","text":"GoogleCloudPubSub wraps the Cloud Pub/Sub REST API.","category":"section"},{"location":"pubsub/#Client","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"Client","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"pubsub/#Emulator","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"Emulator","text":"Set PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST=localhost:8085 (host:port, no scheme) before constructing a PubSubClient and it will use plain HTTP with no authentication.","category":"section"},{"location":"pubsub/#Topics","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"Topics","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"pubsub/#Subscriptions","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"Subscriptions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"pubsub/#Messages","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"Messages","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"pubsub/#Example","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"Example","text":"import GoogleCloudPubSub\n\nps = GoogleCloudPubSub.PubSubClient(project=\"my-project\")\n\n# Topic lifecycle\ntopic = GoogleCloudPubSub.create_topic(ps, \"my-topic\")\nprintln(topic.name)\n\n# Subscription\nsub = GoogleCloudPubSub.create_subscription(ps, \"my-sub\", \"my-topic\"; ack_deadline_seconds=30)\n\n# Publish\nmid = GoogleCloudPubSub.publish(ps, \"my-topic\", \"Hello, Pub/Sub!\")\nprintln(\"Published: \", mid)\n\n# Batch publish\nids = GoogleCloudPubSub.publish(ps, \"my-topic\", [\n    GoogleCloudPubSub.PubSubMessage(\"msg-1\"),\n    GoogleCloudPubSub.PubSubMessage(\"msg-2\"; attributes=Dict(\"priority\" => \"high\")),\n])\n\n# Pull and acknowledge\nmsgs = GoogleCloudPubSub.pull(ps, \"my-sub\"; max_messages=10)\nfor m in msgs\n    println(String(m.data), \"  attrs=\", m.attributes)\nend\nack_ids = [m.ack_id for m in msgs if m.ack_id !== nothing]\nGoogleCloudPubSub.acknowledge(ps, \"my-sub\", ack_ids)\n\n# Clean up\nGoogleCloudPubSub.delete_subscription(ps, \"my-sub\")\nGoogleCloudPubSub.delete_topic(ps, \"my-topic\")","category":"section"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.PubSubClient","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.PubSubClient","text":"PubSubClient(; project, creds=nothing, endpoint=nothing)\nPubSubClient(project; creds=nothing, endpoint=nothing)\n\nA Cloud Pub/Sub REST API client.\n\nIf PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST is set in the environment and endpoint is not explicitly provided, the client targets the emulator with no authentication.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.Topic","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.Topic","text":"Topic\n\nA Cloud Pub/Sub topic. The name field is the fully-qualified resource name: \"projects/{project}/topics/{id}\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.create_topic","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.create_topic","text":"create_topic(client, topic_id) -> Topic\n\nCreate a topic in the configured project.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.get_topic","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.get_topic","text":"get_topic(client, topic_id) -> Topic\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.delete_topic","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.delete_topic","text":"delete_topic(client, topic_id) -> Nothing\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.list_topics","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.list_topics","text":"list_topics(client) -> PagedIterator{Topic}\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.exists","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.exists","text":"exists(topic) -> Bool\n\nReturns whether a Topic object has been resolved to a non-empty resource name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.Subscription","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.Subscription","text":"Subscription\n\nA Cloud Pub/Sub pull subscription. Both name and topic are fully-qualified resource names (\"projects/{project}/subscriptions/{id}\" and \"projects/{project}/topics/{id}\" respectively).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.create_subscription","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.create_subscription","text":"create_subscription(client, subscription_id, topic_id; ack_deadline_seconds=10) -> Subscription\n\nCreate a pull subscription bound to topic_id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.get_subscription","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.get_subscription","text":"get_subscription(client, subscription_id) -> Subscription\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.delete_subscription","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.delete_subscription","text":"delete_subscription(client, subscription_id) -> Nothing\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.list_subscriptions","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.list_subscriptions","text":"list_subscriptions(client) -> PagedIterator{Subscription}\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.PubSubMessage","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.PubSubMessage","text":"PubSubMessage\n\nRepresents a Pub/Sub message. Used both for publishing (only data and attributes are sent) and for receiving (server populates message_id, publish_time, and ack_id).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.publish","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.publish","text":"publish(client, topic_id, data) -> String\npublish(client, topic_id, messages::Vector{PubSubMessage}) -> Vector{String}\n\nPublish one or more messages to a topic. Returns the message ID(s) assigned by the server.\n\ndata may be a Vector{UInt8}, an AbstractString, or a PubSubMessage. The single-message variants return a single message ID as String.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.pull","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.pull","text":"pull(client, subscription_id; max_messages=10, return_immediately=true) -> Vector{PubSubMessage}\n\nPull up to max_messages messages from a subscription. Returned messages include an ack_id field which must be passed to acknowledge to permanently remove them from the subscription.\n\nTransient errors (429/5xx) are retried automatically; under Pub/Sub's at-least-once semantics a retried pull may leave messages from the failed attempt leased until their ack deadline expires.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"pubsub/#GoogleCloudPubSub.acknowledge","page":"Cloud Pub/Sub","title":"GoogleCloudPubSub.acknowledge","text":"acknowledge(client, subscription_id, ack_ids::Vector{<:AbstractString}) -> Nothing\n\nAcknowledge one or more messages so the server stops redelivering them. Transient errors (429/5xx) are retried automatically — re-acking an already acknowledged message is harmless.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#storage","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"Cloud Storage API","text":"GoogleCloudStorage wraps the GCS JSON API.","category":"section"},{"location":"storage/#Client","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"Client","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"storage/#Emulator","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"Emulator","text":"Set STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST=http://localhost:4443 (or any http:// URL) before constructing a Client and it will skip authentication automatically.","category":"section"},{"location":"storage/#Bucket-operations","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"Bucket operations","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"storage/#Object-operations","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"Object operations","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"storage/#Example","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"Example","text":"import GoogleCloudStorage\n\ngcs = GoogleCloudStorage.Client(\"my-project\")\n\n# Bucket lifecycle\nbucket = GoogleCloudStorage.create_bucket(gcs, \"my-bucket\"; location=\"US\")\nprintln(bucket.name)\n\n# Upload / download\nGoogleCloudStorage.upload_object(gcs, \"my-bucket\", \"hello.txt\", \"Hello World!\")\nbytes = GoogleCloudStorage.download_object(gcs, \"my-bucket\", \"hello.txt\")\nprintln(String(bytes))   # \"Hello World!\"\n\n# List objects under a prefix\nfor obj in GoogleCloudStorage.list_objects(gcs, \"my-bucket\"; prefix=\"logs/\")\n    println(obj.name, \"  \", obj.size, \" bytes\")\nend\n\n# Clean up\nGoogleCloudStorage.delete_object(gcs, \"my-bucket\", \"hello.txt\")\nGoogleCloudStorage.delete_bucket(gcs, \"my-bucket\")","category":"section"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.Client","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.Client","text":"Client(project_id; creds=nothing, endpoint=nothing)\n\nA Google Cloud Storage JSON API client.\n\nIf STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST is set in the environment and endpoint is not provided, the client targets the emulator with no authentication.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.Bucket","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.Bucket","text":"Bucket\n\nMetadata for a Google Cloud Storage bucket.\n\nFields: name, location (e.g. \"US\"), storage_class (e.g. \"STANDARD\").\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.list_buckets","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.list_buckets","text":"list_buckets(client) -> PagedIterator{Bucket}\n\nIterate over all buckets belonging to the client's project.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.get_bucket","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.get_bucket","text":"get_bucket(client, name) -> Bucket\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.create_bucket","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.create_bucket","text":"create_bucket(client, name; location=\"US\", storage_class=\"STANDARD\") -> Bucket\n\nCreate a new GCS bucket in the client's project.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.delete_bucket","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.delete_bucket","text":"delete_bucket(client, name)\n\nDelete a GCS bucket. The bucket must be empty.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.Object","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.Object","text":"Object\n\nMetadata for an object stored in Google Cloud Storage.\n\nFields: bucket, name, size (bytes), content_type, generation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.list_objects","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.list_objects","text":"list_objects(client, bucket; prefix=nothing) -> PagedIterator{Object}\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.get_object","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.get_object","text":"get_object(client, bucket, name) -> Object\n\nFetch object metadata (does not download the object body).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.download_object","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.download_object","text":"download_object(client, bucket, name) -> Vector{UInt8}\ndownload_object(client, bucket, name, io) -> Nothing\n\nFetch the object body. The second form writes bytes into the provided IO.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.upload_object","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.upload_object","text":"upload_object(client, bucket, name, data; content_type=\"application/octet-stream\") -> Object\n\nSimple (non-resumable) upload. data may be Vector{UInt8}, AbstractString, or IO. Uses uploadType=media — for large payloads, prefer a resumable upload (planned for v0.2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"storage/#GoogleCloudStorage.delete_object","page":"Cloud Storage","title":"GoogleCloudStorage.delete_object","text":"delete_object(client, bucket, name)\n\nDelete an object from a bucket.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"contributing/#contributing","page":"Contributing","title":"Contributing","text":"This page is for maintainers and contributors. It covers the repository layout, local development setup, and how AI assistance was used in this project.","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#Repository-layout","page":"Contributing","title":"Repository layout","text":"GoogleCloudAPIs.jl/\n├── GoogleAuth.jl/          # Auth sub-package\n│   ├── src/\n│   └── test/\n├── GoogleApiCore.jl/       # Shared HTTP/pagination infrastructure\n├── GoogleCloudStorage.jl/  # GCS sub-package\n├── BigQuery.jl/            # BigQuery sub-package\n├── GoogleCloudPubSub.jl/   # Pub/Sub sub-package\n├── docs/                   # Documenter.jl source\n├── .github/workflows/      # CI (CI.yml, Docs.yml, TagBot.yml, CompatHelper.yml)\n├── docker-compose.yml      # Local emulator stack\n└── Project.toml            # Root dev environment (not a package itself)\n\nEach sub-package is an independent Julia package with its own Project.toml, src/, and test/ directories. The root Project.toml is a dev-only environment for running all tests from one place.","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#Local-development-setup","page":"Contributing","title":"Local development setup","text":"# From the repo root\nusing Pkg\nPkg.develop([\n    PackageSpec(path=\"GoogleAuth.jl\"),\n    PackageSpec(path=\"GoogleApiCore.jl\"),\n    PackageSpec(path=\"GoogleCloudStorage.jl\"),\n    PackageSpec(path=\"BigQuery.jl\"),\n    PackageSpec(path=\"GoogleCloudPubSub.jl\"),\n])\nPkg.instantiate()","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#Running-tests","page":"Contributing","title":"Running tests","text":"Unit and mock tests (no emulators needed):\n\n# Run all packages\nPkg.test(\"GoogleAuth\")\nPkg.test(\"GoogleApiCore\")\n\nIntegration tests (requires emulators):\n\ndocker compose up -d\n\nThen run the relevant package test. The test suites auto-detect emulator env vars:\n\nEnv var Default Package\nSTORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST http://localhost:4443 GoogleCloudStorage\nBIGQUERY_EMULATOR_HOST http://localhost:9050 BigQuery\nPUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST localhost:8085 GoogleCloudPubSub\n\nIf the env var is not set, each test suite attempts to start a Docker container automatically and falls back to skipping integration tests if Docker is unavailable.","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#Adding-a-new-sub-package","page":"Contributing","title":"Adding a new sub-package","text":"Create NewPackage.jl/ with the standard layout (src/, test/, Project.toml).\nAdd GoogleApiCore and GoogleAuth as deps if needed.\nAdd the package to the root Project.toml deps and the Pkg.develop lists in CI.yml and docs/make.jl.\nAdd a corresponding docs/src/newpackage.md and register it in docs/make.jl's pages.\nAdd a test matrix entry in CI.yml.","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#Release-process","page":"Contributing","title":"Release process","text":"Bump version in the sub-package's Project.toml.\nPush to main. TagBot creates the git tag automatically after the General registry PR merges.\nRegister with Registrator by commenting on any commit:\n@JuliaRegistrator register subdir=NewPackage.jl","category":"section"},{"location":"contributing/#AI-assisted-development","page":"Contributing","title":"AI-assisted development","text":"This library was developed with significant assistance from Claude (Anthropic). Per the Julia General Registry policy on LLM use, the following areas had substantial AI involvement:\n\nArea LLM involvement\nPackage architecture Monorepo structure and sub-package separation were designed with AI assistance\nSource code (src/) All implementation files were co-written with Claude; logic was reviewed and tested by the human author\nTest suites (test/) Mock HTTP server approach and test case design were AI-generated; integration tests were verified against real emulators\nCI/CD GitHub Actions workflows, emulator health checks, and CompatHelper / TagBot setup were generated with AI assistance\nDocumentation Initial docstrings and this documentation were AI-drafted and edited by the human author\n\nAll generated code has been read, understood, and validated by the human maintainer through CI, emulator integration tests, and manual testing against real GCP services.","category":"section"},{"location":"#GoogleCloudAPIs.jl","page":"Home","title":"GoogleCloudAPIs.jl","text":"Julia client libraries for Google Cloud Platform.","category":"section"},{"location":"#Packages","page":"Home","title":"Packages","text":"Package Description\nGoogleAuth ADC, service account JWT, OAuth 2.0 browser flow\nGoogleApiCore HTTP retry, pagination, long-running operations\nGoogleCloudStorage Cloud Storage JSON API\nBigQuery BigQuery REST API\nGoogleCloudPubSub Cloud Pub/Sub REST API\n\nFor installation and quick-start examples, see the README.\n\nFor contributing, repo structure, and development setup, see Contributing.","category":"section"}]
}
